+  statement: "For x̂ ∈ T̂ = {x̂ ≥ 0 : S ≤ τ, ρ₁ ≤ C(s)}: (x̂, u) ∈ T̃ ⇔ 0 ≤ u ≤ U(x̂) = min{L − S, max{g, C(s+1) − ρ₁}}; the fibre is empty off T̂ (cap step from m = 1 and C(0) ≥ 0); Definition 4.6's marginal of 1_{T̃} P equals J_T(P) for continuous P; ∫₀^U (M − u)^p u^t du in closed form"
+  source: "Source/bgp212.pdf: Definition 4.1, Definition 4.6, Table 3 (p. 39), §9.4 and Lemma 9.2, Theorem 11.1"
